Licenses for the artwork in this directory
==========================================

The source code of this project is under the MIT License (see ../LICENSE).
The artwork below is not; each set keeps the license of its upstream, and the
sets are aggregated here, not merged into a single work.

pidgin-2.10.12-pixmaps/
-----------------------

The "Default" smiley theme from Pidgin 2.10.12 (theme author Hylke Bons).
Licensed under the GNU General Public License, version 2 or later; the full
text is in COPYING.

The 24x24 PNG files under
../hiroba-server/src/main/webapp/com.liquable.hiroba/emoji/pidgin/ are
rendered from the SVG files in pidgin-2.10.12-pixmaps/emotes/default/24/
scalable/ and are distributed under the same license.

emoji_one_2016_01_29_svg/ and emoji_one_category_icons/
------------------------------------------------------

Emoji artwork is provided by Emojitwo (https://emojitwo.github.io/),
originally released as Emojione 2.2 (https://www.emojione.com) by Ranks.com
(http://www.ranks.com) with contributions from the Emojitwo community and is
licensed under CC-BY 4.0
(https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/legalcode).

Modified: the SVG files were rendered to 24x24 and 48x48 PNG (emoji) and to
16x16 and 32x32 PNG (category icons). The rendered files are under
../hiroba-server/src/main/webapp/com.liquable.hiroba/emoji/emoji_one/ and
.../emoji/category/ and are distributed under the same license.

image_work/
-----------

Working files for the interface icons in
../hiroba-transport/src/main/java/com/liquable/hiroba/gwt/client/res/img/.

media-playback-start.svg is from the Tango Icon Theme, by Lapo Calamandrei
with Jakub Steiner, released into the public domain. media-playback-start.png,
down.png and up.png are derived from it, and down.png and up.png are also
shipped in the res/img directory named above.

gnome_window_close.png is the window-close icon of the GNOME icon theme. The
icon ships only in the 3.x releases of that theme, whose COPYING reads: "GNOME
icon theme is distributed under the terms of either GNU LGPL v.3 or Creative
Commons BY-SA 3.0 license."
(https://www.gnu.org/licenses/lgpl-3.0.html,
https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/3.0/). The file carries no embedded
metadata, so the release it came from is not recorded. This project uses it
under CC BY-SA 3.0. deleteMedia.png and deleteMediaSelf.png are derived from it,
are shipped in the res/img directory named above, and are distributed under
CC BY-SA 3.0 as well.
